{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the responsibility chain: it repeatedly checked respiratory/PE and bleeding red flags, framed the diagnosis as suspected rather than confirmed/excluded PE, reconciled anticoagulation execution, used available records/family-provided wording, and converted staged results into bedside and discharge plans. It also completed multiple high-order opportunities: real-world workflow scripting, reconciliation of medication/test mismatches, correction of anticoagulation/D-dimer misconceptions, and dynamic response to activity-related dyspnea/discharge risk. Closure was safe and executable because the caregiver had a clear home plan for rivaroxaban, oxygen, pending imaging/follow-up, and emergency thresholds. No important non-chain defect or responsibility-chain error is evident, so the deterministic boundary supports grade 5.",
